    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d687-a1">

                <pb facs="0669" n="1403" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1403"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 728.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Tevfik Pasha to Mr. Terrell.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Ministry of Foreign Affairs, Sublime
                            Porte</hi></placeName>,<lb/><date calendar="gregorian" when="1895-12-02"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">December 2,
                    1895</hi>.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Envoy</hi>: In reply to the note your excellency
                    has kindly addressed to me on the 18th ultimo, No. 99, I hasten to inform you
                    that the Sublime Porte, which had already invited the provincial authorities to
                    use the greatest vigilance for the protection of all the foreign subjects in the
                    Empire, has just renewed to the said authorities, in the most earnest manner,
                    its instructions in the same sense.</p>
                <p>Please accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tevfik.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
